    "narrative": "Our offensive core faces a mixed bag of matchups today, but **Christian Yelich** stands out as the premier play with a 73.63 efficiency score. He draws a favorable matchup against Singer, where a strong platoon edge (+13%) and a spot in the heart of the order push him into our elite tier. Similarly, **Junior Caminero** (66.33) and **Lars Nootbaar** (65.16) anchor the lineup; **Lars Nootbaar** benefits significantly from the leadoff spot and a +11% platoon advantage against Rocker, while **Junior Caminero** remains a daily staple due to his high base projection and consistent order placement. Despite facing the formidable Skenes, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** maintains a high 64.88 score; his dynamic platoon edge and the +10% order bonus effectively neutralize the SP skill penalty, making his stolen base upside essential for our 5x5 objectives.\n\nThe decision-making process at the bottom of the order was tight, ultimately pushing **Kazuma Okamoto** (57.47) and **Josh Smith** (57.97) into the lineup while sidelining **Chase Meidroth**. **Chase Meidroth** fell just short of our 40.0 floor at 39.88, as his unfavorable park and SP skill metrics couldn't overcome the negative platoon weighting. Meanwhile, we are monitoring the risk profile of **Pete Crow-Armstrong** closely; while his speed is a differentiator, the presence of an elite catcher and the hold-risk against his aggressive base-running style warrants caution. Outside of our active starters, **Yordan Alvarez** and **Gary Sanchez** remain unavailable, and **Casey Schmitt** continues to occupy an IL slot, leaving us to rely on our secondary speed threats like **Caleb Durbin** to keep pace in the SB category against a manageable Dobnak matchup.",
